<template>
    <heading>Project State Machine</heading>
    <keywords><li>startup</li><li>state machine</li><li>project selection</li></keywords>
    <section data-lp5-kind="explanation">
        <p>This little-language source defines the startup command flow. The base state calls the Select/Create dialog state. Displaying the dialog is one-time state entry code, not a repeatable ModalDialog handler. Its Select command calls the selection state, whose entry code starts the private async picker/loading function. Calls preserve the completion command, so success closes the dialog while picker abort permits retry.</p>
        <p>Selection entry code starts async work during the Select click. Only <code>ProjectLoaded</code> and <code>ProjectPickerAborted</code> are accepted while that work is pending; all other commands are ignored. These compiled states use only calls, ordinary waits, and returns, which the unchanged controller already supports. Rendering and project creation remain unfinished.</p>
        <p>Indentation rule for humans and agents: every directive's first token is right-justified at column 5. Thus <code>state</code> starts at column 1, <code>on</code> and <code>-&gt;</code> at column 4, and <code>-&gt;()</code> at column 2; their right-hand sides all start at column 7. Keep directives in that left-hand column even inside JavaScript conditions, so the state and transition structure can be read vertically. Indent ordinary JavaScript separately; directive indentation has no semantic effect.</p>
    </section>
    <section data-lp5-kind="code">
        <name>Project state machine</name>
        <code><![CDATA[
const stateMachineSource = `
state baseOperationsHandler
   on ModalDialog
        if (event.dialogName === "SelectCreateProject") {
 ->() SelectCreateProject
        }

state SelectCreateProject
        view.showModalDialog("SelectCreateProject");

   on SelectProject
 ->() SelectProject
        if (event.name === "ProjectLoaded") {
            view.closeModalDialog("SelectCreateProject");
            // TODO: Ask the view to render the loaded model.
            return;
        }

state SelectProject
        asyncSelectProject(event);

   on ProjectLoaded
        return;

   on ProjectPickerAborted
        return;
`;
]]></code></section></template>
